        {
          "path": "_m/w/6/v/4/japanese-bridge-wp/a-final-look-at-the-fascinatin.jpg",
          "filename": "A final look at the fascinating Japanese Bridge (31654247472).jpg",
          "caption": "Back outside, here is a final look at the Japanese Covered Bridge in the Hoi An old quarter before we move on. It is hard to believe that some Philistine actually flattened the road surface of the bridge to allow passage of cars. Fortunately, better sense prevailed in 1986 when the original arch was restored and the bridge closed to vehicular traffic. According to the Lonely Planet website, the bridge is once again scheduled to close for repairs and restoration though the dates have not been announced yet. It certainly did appear in fine fettle when I visited.(Hoi An, Central Vietnam, Nov. 2016)",
          "alt": "Back outside, here is a final look at the Japanese Covered Bridge in the Hoi An old quarter before we move on. It is hard to believe that some Philistine actually flattened the road surface of the bridge to allow passage of cars. Fortunately, better sense prevailed in 1986 when the original arch was restored and the bridge closed to vehicular traffic. According to the Lonely Planet website, the bridge is once again scheduled to close for repairs and restoration though the dates have not been announced yet. It certainly did appear in fine fettle when I visited.(Hoi An, Central Vietnam, Nov. 2016)",
          "width": 6000,
          "height": 4000,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_final_look_at_the_fascinating_Japanese_Bridge_(31654247472).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
